From 6dd145a5bb80d6e52d1d4376e5ad24ef6751dd76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Zakharov <contact@zalexdev.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 22:00:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] um: arm64: add the port's README and test harness

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. This commit exists so that a published tree is
self-contained; it is deliberately the last one, so the series meant for
review is origin/next..HEAD~1 and does not contain it.

The README states what works and what does not, and the harness is how
every claim in it was checked: gate boots that decide on a marker string
rather than an exit status, a phone runner that captures on the device
because streaming loses the tail, and a benchmark that measures several
kernels inside one interleaved run and voids its own table when a
pure-userspace validator says the machine moved between conditions.

Sources only -- no images, no compiled probes, no built binaries.

Signed-off-by: Oleksii Zakharov <contact@zalexdev.com>
